out the langchain4j-typesafe-ai maven dependency and Jev model:\n\n## Jev Model Overview\n\nJev is a System One model from TypeSafe AI that takes unstructured program state plus typed questions and returns typed answers with calibrated probabilities. It does not generate text.\n\nJev is a new model from TypeSafe AI, released on September 15, 2026 alongside a $40 million seed round led by DCVC.\n\n## LangChain4j Integration\n\nThis adds models/langchain4j-community-typesafe, a Java integration for TypeSafe AI's System One API and its default jev-latest model. TypeSafeJudgeModel implements the new core JudgeModel contract, sends all named questions in one POST /v1/systemone request, and maps noul, choice, and score results back to JudgeAnswer values.\n\n## Question Types\n\nThree question types cover the surface: Choice picks from options, Score rates against ordered levels, Noul answers yes or no.\n\nFor the specific Maven dependency details, the search results show this is part of the langchain4j-community project, but the exact dependency coordinates and version number would be available in the Maven Central Repository or the official LangChain4j documentation."],"durationSeconds":6.705484333001078,"searchCount":1}}